:false,"_score_mult_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.08805648965727798,"_gp_fcf_yield":true,"_score_fcf_yield":60.5,"_gate_int_coverage":1.6935109359248814,"_gp_int_coverage":false,"_score_int_coverage":3.7,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":4.8100761810688075,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":0.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.18962309120306606,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":95.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.20892425806146667,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":54.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.10402078336257317,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.2471165043079619,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":100.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.2821023766991562,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.017539118958018587,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":10.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.037404438155853856,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":20.9,"_gate_pool_share":-0.19757623242101585,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.13992780525117254,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":95.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.23998811343817894,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.000313746421551786,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":50.3,"_gate_fund_growth":0.11735674523853304,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07778679468632603,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":97.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.04545878689039562,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009082951319429784,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.03159,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":21.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.174,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":17.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"Crocs, Inc. together with its subsidiaries, designs, develops, manufactures, markets, distributes, and sells casual lifestyle footwear and accessories for men, women, and kids under the Crocs and HEYDUDE Brands in the United States and internationally. The company offers various footwear products, including clogs, sandals, loafers, classics, fuzz, platforms, boots, sandals, slides, slippers, sneakers, flip flops, and flats, as well as totes, backpacks, belt bags, socks, bag charms, cases, attachments, cartoon characters products, and touchland and other accessories. It sells its products through wholesalers, retail stores, e-commerce sites, third-party marketplaces, outlet stores, and kiosks/store-in-store locations. Crocs, Inc. was founded in 1999 and is headquartered in Broomfield, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Andrew  Rees | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $504K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Crocs, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $7.5B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 34% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 25-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 52% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $659M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9703019303745255},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (83% sell ratio, net $20.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 38% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Crocs (NASDAQ:CROX) Sets New 12-Month High \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/crocs-nasdaqcrox-sets-new-12-month-high-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794597687.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is It Worth Investing in Crocs (CROX) Based on Wall Street's Bullish Views?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/worth-investing-crocs-crox-based-133005024.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576605.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.821,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Did HEYDUDE's Return to Growth Help CROX (NASDAQ:CROX) Raise Its Outlook Again?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/how-did-heydudes-return-to-growth-help-crox-nasdaqcrox-raise-its-outlook-again","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Marvel x Crocs Doctor Doom Classic Clog Release Date","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/marvel-x-crocs-doctor-doom-213200000.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794616434.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Mariah Carey Fans 'Genuinely Concerned' After Viral Video Appears to Capture the Singer 'Struggling to Walk': Watch","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/mariah-carey-fans-genuinely-concerned-2